1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,717
This guide covers the new reset and saving controls in Circuit Studio.

2
00:00:04,917 --> 00:00:08,522
The same controls work for both CS and CE labs.

3
00:00:08,722 --> 00:00:13,266
You will learn how to restart a circuit, recover it, and save evidence of your work.

4
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:18,262
In your lab, choose Reset circuit in the footer or the workspace toolbar.

5
00:00:18,462 --> 00:00:23,497
It restores the initial unwired parts, their positions, and their starting values.

6
00:00:23,697 --> 00:00:26,961
The current breadboard assembly is cleared so you can rebuild.

7
00:00:27,161 --> 00:00:28,825
Your report notes stay saved.

8
00:00:29,725 --> 00:00:33,543
If you want the circuit you had before resetting, choose Undo reset.

9
00:00:33,743 --> 00:00:36,709
This restores that circuit and its saved breadboard.

10
00:00:36,909 --> 00:00:39,597
Reset and undo apply to the selected lab.

11
00:00:39,797 --> 00:00:42,591
Your CS and CE work are kept separately.

12
00:00:43,491 --> 00:00:49,294
For a file you can reopen and edit, choose Save views, then Save editable project JSON.

13
00:00:49,494 --> 00:00:51,734
You can also use File, then Save As.

14
00:00:51,934 --> 00:00:58,462
A saved image or document is evidence of the view; the project file preserves the editable design.

15
00:00:59,362 --> 00:01:01,645
In Save views, choose Circuit schematic.

16
00:01:01,845 --> 00:01:04,213
Save PNG image creates a picture.

17
00:01:04,413 --> 00:01:11,154
Save PDF creates a PDF file, and Save Word creates a Word document containing the captured
view.

18
00:01:11,354 --> 00:01:13,914
Choose the format required for your assignment.

19
00:01:14,814 --> 00:01:19,422
Before saving simulation evidence, press Run and wait for the current results.

20
00:01:19,622 --> 00:01:22,673
In Save views, choose Simulation display and settings.

21
00:01:22,873 --> 00:01:26,563
The export includes the displayed result and instrument settings.

22
00:01:26,763 --> 00:01:30,561
If results are out of date, run the simulation again before saving.

23
00:01:31,461 --> 00:01:34,767
Open the breadboard workspace before saving its assembly.

24
00:01:34,967 --> 00:01:37,805
Choose Save views, then Breadboard and instruments.

25
00:01:38,005 --> 00:01:41,077
Save the image, PDF, or Word file you need.

26
00:01:41,277 --> 00:01:46,269
The export reflects the parts, jumpers, instruments, and power state currently shown.

27
00:01:46,469 --> 00:01:48,709
Use your own construction as evidence.

28
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:53,022
Choose All available views to combine the views that are ready.

29
00:01:53,222 --> 00:01:57,105
PDF and Word place each included view on its own page.

30
00:01:57,305 --> 00:02:01,379
The PNG option combines the included views into one image.

31
00:02:01,579 --> 00:02:04,481
Read the save status to see which views were included.

32
00:02:05,381 --> 00:02:10,735
Open your saved files and check that the labels, scales, and input settings are readable.

33
00:02:10,935 --> 00:02:14,669
Keep the editable project and a Save progress backup as well.

34
00:02:14,869 --> 00:02:20,849
Upload your required evidence and report through the class site, with separate CS and CE

35
00:02:20,849 --> 00:02:21,247
submissions.
